abstract={This paper focuses on the turning maneuverability of a bionic gliding robotic dolphin. Inspired by natural dolphin's turning styles, a novel gliding robotic dolphin with a special yaw joint is developed to purse high turning maneuverability. Thus, the robot can realize several turning patterns based on its flippers, yaw joint and dolphin-like dorsal-abdominal undulating mechanism. Considering both dolphin-like mode and gliding mode, a dynamic model is constructed to further analyze the turning performance through adopting the Newton-Euler method. Thereafter, five turning patterns are selected to explore how the special mechanism as well as some key parameters affect the turning performance of the robotic dolphin. The simulation results reveal that every pattern can successfully and effectively realize turning motions, furthermore, appropriate turning pattern as well as control parameters can contribute to high maneuverability, i.e., small turning radius and high turning velocity, which provides valuable guidance for future control and application of the bionic gliding robotic dolphin. © 2021 IEEE.},
