abstract={Taking as signal model the sum of a non-stationnary deterministic part embedded in a white Gaussian noise, this paper presents the distribution of the coefficients of the Short Time Fourier Transform (STFT), which is used to determine the maximum likelihood estimator of the noise level. We then propose an automatic segmentation algorithm of the real and imaginary parts of the STFT based on statistical features, which is an alternative to the spectrogram segmentations considered as image segmentations. Examples of segmented time-frequency space are presented on a simulated signal and on a dolphin whistle. © 2006 IEEE.},
