abstract={The 3 approaches correspond to parameter estimation for 3 population growth models. Parameter estimation for the Leslie matrix and geometric series models are based only on known-aged individuals. The birth-interval model is developed making fuller use of available information. The birth-interval approach uses only known-aged individuals to estimate the first-birth ogive and uses all females with previous births to estimate the probabilities associated with various birth intervals. A Monte-Carlo simulation is used to examine the bias and precision of the 3 methods given the quantity of data that is usually available in a multiple resighting study. All 3 approaches appear capable of giving unbiased estimates of population growth rate. -from Author},
