abstract={The abstract refers to two computer simulation models which translate the results of trajectory models into either short or long term estimates of changes in population size resulting from oil spill related mortality. The short term oil response model (STORM), simulates the daily pattern of behavior and geograhic distribution of a species. Estimates of the long term effects of oil development are made using the oil spill population response model, OSPREY. This model projects population size and composition from year to year based on age-specific fecundity and mortality. Output from the STORM model is used to modify estimates of annual mortality, simulating the effects of oil development. OSPREY is used to estimate the probability that the population size will be reduced as a result of offshore oil development, and how large that reduction is likely to be.},
