abstract={The colloquium discussed the problem of ship collision with bridges, and offshore structures. Case histories and statistics are detailed. Navigational aspects such as traffic flows, risk management and the role of ship simulation in dredging safe bridge and offshore structures were examined. Evaluation of collision probability and risk assessment methods were studied and determination of impact forces examined. Damage may be reduced by protective structures such as artificial islands rubble mound structures against bridge piers floating systems, systems with piles, fixed or sliding dolphins with or without fenders. Design and modelling of these structures are discussed. Acceptable levels of risk for bridges etc. were studied and a comprehensive design approach to bridges over navigation channels/navigable waters presented. (C.J.U.)},
